            <ArticleTitle>Fungemia and interstitial lung compromise caused by Malassezia sympodialis in a pediatric patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>118-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.riam.2014.01.002</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1130-1406(14)00040-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of fungemia with interstitial lung compromise caused by Malassezia sympodialis is reported in an obese pediatric patient on long-term treatment with inhaled corticosteroids for asthma. The patient was hospitalized due to a post-surgical complication of appendicitis. The patient was treated with amphotericin B for 3 weeks, with good clinical evolution and subsequent negative cultures.</AbstractText>
